    {
      "name": "llama.cpp server",
      "match": {
        "port": 8080,
        "server": "llama.cpp"
      },
      "dialect": "openai-chat",
      "as_of": "2026-10-26",
      "src": "https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/blob/master/tools/server/README.md",
      "note": "System messages and roles go through the model's own chat template, so a template that enforces alternation (Mistral, Gemma) is narrowed back by models.json. A trailing assistant message is continued (prefill). The last stream chunk carries `timings` (prompt_n, predicted_n, cache_n) whether or not stream_options is sent. cache_prompt:true keeps the slot's KV prefix (agents never send false, §7.4.7). response_format json_schema is said to become a grammar, but a local server's structured output counts only once a probe (rp-core probe --active) or the user confirms it (§7.2), so it is not claimed here. Capacity is NOT taken from -np / total_slots [D-84].",
      "caps": {
        "midSystem": "native",
        "alternation": "free",
        "prefill": "assistant-last",
        "parallelToolCalls": "send-true",
        "samplers": {
          "accepted": [
            "temperature",
            "top_p",
            "top_k",
            "min_p",
            "typical_p",
            "repetition_penalty",
            "frequency_penalty",
            "presence_penalty",
            "seed",
            "stop",
            "max_tokens"
          ],
          "wire": {
            "repetition_penalty": "repeat_penalty"
          }
        },
        "streamUsage": "timings",
        "caching": "auto-prefix",
        "extraBody": {
          "cache_prompt": true
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "Ollama",
      "match": {
        "port": 11434,
        "server": "ollama"
      },
      "dialect": "openai-chat",
      "as_of": "2026-10-26",
      "src": "https://docs.ollama.com/api/openai-compatibility",
      "note": "/v1/chat/completions supports model, messages, frequency_penalty, presence_penalty, response_format, seed, stop, stream, stream_options.include_usage, temperature, top_p, max_tokens, tools, reasoning_effort / reasoning.effort; tool_choice, logit_bias, user and n are unsupported. top_k / min_p / repeat_penalty exist only as options of the native /api/chat, so they are not claimed here. 'The OpenAI API does not have a way of setting the context size': the window is num_ctx (Modelfile PARAMETER num_ctx or the server default), not model_info context_length (see probe.ts). response_format json_schema is documented, but a local server's structured output counts only once a probe (rp-core probe --active) or the user confirms it (§7.2).",
      "caps": {
        "toolChoiceHonored": false,
        "prefill": "assistant-last",
        "samplers": {
          "accepted": [
            "temperature",
            "top_p",
            "frequency_penalty",
            "presence_penalty",
            "seed",
            "stop",
            "max_tokens"
          ]
        },
        "streamUsage": "stream_options",
        "caching": "auto-prefix"
      }
    },
