      "name": "OpenRouter",
      "match": {
        "hostname": "openrouter.ai",
        "server": "openrouter"
      },
      "dialect": "openai-chat",
      "as_of": "2026-10-26",
      "src": "https://openrouter.ai/docs/api-reference/parameters; https://openrouter.ai/docs/use-cases/usage-accounting; Bunraku:src/kit/providers/spokes/openrouter.ts@702d8120 (stop 4); RoleCall:apps/rc/src/lib/providers/adapters/openai.ts@fb8dc623e (provider.allow_fallbacks, no volatile metadata)",
      "note": "provider.allow_fallbacks:false keeps the request on the chosen provider (RoleCall; volatile metadata would break the prefix cache, so none is sent). Usage is always in the last SSE message; usage.include and stream_options are deprecated no-ops. Reasoning comes as `reasoning` plus structured `reasoning_details`, which tool loops send back (§8.6). Reasoning control, tools and structured outputs come per model from the catalog's supported_parameters; no disable is sent unless a row allows it (grok-4.5 answers it with 400).",
      "caps": {
        "extraBody": {
          "provider": {
            "allow_fallbacks": false
